        "geo_confidence": "high",
        "entwurfsbeschreibung": "ELEMENTA is important as a housing proposal organised around the reuse of substantial existing components. The architectural interest lies in how salvaged concrete and other building elements can discipline a new residential scheme: bay spacing, stair logic, facade rhythm and construction sequence all have to negotiate availability. Because delivery status still needs verification, the description should remain design-focused. It is a project about making component reuse compatible with ordinary collective housing, not about a one-off pavilion gesture.",
